ook XI”, in Paradise Lost. […], 2nd edition, London: […] S[amuel] Simmons […], →OCLC, pages 299–300:"}, {"text": "This night shall see the gaudy wreath decline, The roses wither and the lilies pine.", "reference": "170?, Thomas Tickell, To a Lady; With a Present of Flowers:"}, {"text": "The way the story went was that the man's foot healed up all right but that he just pined away.", "reference": "1994, Walter Dean Myers, The Glory Field, →ISBN, page 29:"}, {"text": "Before I pine away (Pine away)", "reference": "2001 May 15, Tool, “Reflection” (track 11), in Lateralus:"}], "synonyms": ["languish", "droop"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(intransitive) To long, to yearn so much that it causes suffering.", "tags": ["intransitive"], "examples": ["Laura was pining for Bill all the time he was gone."], "quotes": [{"text": "Praline: \"That parrot is definitely deceased. And when I bought it not half an hour ago you assured me that its lack of movement was due to it being tired and shagged out after a long squawk.\"\nShopkeeper: \"It's probably pining for the fiords.\"\nPraline: \"Pining for the fiords, what kind of talk is that?\"", "reference": "1969 December 7, Monty Python, “Full Frontal Nudity, Dead Parrot sketch”, in Monty Python's Flying Circus, spoken by shopkeeper and Mr Praline (Michael Palin and John Cleese):"}, {"text": "Ten years ago, liberals pined for a post-religious right, a different culture war. Be careful what you wish for.", "reference": "2016 August 14, Ross Douthat, “A Playboy for President”, in The New York Times:"}, {"text": "Of the group, Max (Room’s Jacob Tremblay) is the most nominally mature, at least biologically speaking; unlike his childhood companions, he’s entered the early throes of puberty, and spends a lot of his waking hours pining, rather chastely, for a classmate (Millie Davis).", "reference": "2019 August 14, A. A. Dowd, “Good Boys Puts a Tween Spin on the R-rated Teen Comedy, to Mostly Funny Effect”, in The A.V. Club, archived from the original on 04 Mar 2021:"}], "synonyms": ["long", "yearn"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(transitive) To grieve or mourn for.", "tags": ["transitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": ["bewail", "lament", "afterthink", "becry", "begrieve", "bemoan", "bemourn", "bewail", "beweep", "condole", "deplore", "elegize", "grieve", "grieven", "keen", "lament", "mean", "mourn", "pine", "repent", "sigh", "sorrow", "wail", "wayment"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "оплаквам"}, {"language": {"code": "zh", "name": "Chinese Mandarin"}, "word": "悼念"}, {"language": {"code": "nl", "name": "Dutch"}, "word": "treuren"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "ikävöidä"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "surra"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "trauern"}, {"language": {"code": "mi", "name": "Māori"}, "word": "hiangongo"}, {"language": {"code": "mi", "name": "Māori"}, "word": "whakamomori"}, {"language": {"code": "mi", "name": "Māori"}, "word": "konau"}, {"language": {"code": "pl", "name": "Polish"}, "word": "opłakiwać"}, {"language": {"code": "pl", "name": "Polish"}, "word": "obchodzić żałobę"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "añorar"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(transitive) To inflict pain upon; to torment.", "tags": ["transitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Which way, O Lord, which way can I look, and not see some sad examples of misery? […] [O]ne is pined in prison; another, tortured on the rack; a third, languisheth under the loss of a dear son, or wife, or husband.", "reference": "1648, Joseph Hall, “The Breathings of the Devout Soul”, in Josiah Pratt, editor, The Works of the Right Reverend Father in God, Joseph Hall, D.D. […], volume VI (Devotional Works), London: […] C[harles] Whittingham, […]; for Williams and Smith, […], published 1808, →OCLC, page 325:"}], "synonyms": ["afflict", "torment", "torture", "ache", "afflict", "aggrieve", "agonize", "anguish", "dere", "excruciate", "hurt", "irritate", "pang", "pine", "rack", "throe", "torment", "torture", "wring"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pine", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}}}}